    "updated_at": "2026-11-24T04:29:39Z",
    "body": "Scope addition from a second review of PR #3818 (posted after the merge). The ring law of #3818 also changes the output of **2D Adaptive Spiral**, with \"Pass starts at\" Inside or Outside round a part. The paths are `pocket.rs:351-354` with `generate.rs:997`, and `pocket_avoid.rs:254-259`. No pin covers this, and the PR has no changelog row for it. The links are still proved, so the change does not gouge.\n\nThe class fix that the review asks for: one ring-strategy predicate (`Waterline | OffsetRings`), used at both places, so that the ring law applies only to the ring strategies that this rule covers. This issue now also covers 2D Adaptive Spiral. Either keep it out of the ring law by that predicate, or pin it as for the 2D Pocket. Record the choice.\n",
    "author_association": "OWNER",
    "pin": null,
